## Unity UI workflow (UI Agent Tools) - mandatory for any prefab/scene change

All commands go through the wrapper in the project root. It works whether Unity is open
(it talks to the running Editor) or closed (it starts Unity in batch mode):
`./ui-agent.sh <command>` (macOS/Linux/Git Bash) or `.\ui-agent.cmd <command>` (Windows).
Every command prints a RESULT line and exits non-zero on failure. Treat failure as "not done".

| Command | Use |
|---|---|
| `map [asset]` | Regenerate UIAgentMap (all, or one `.prefab`/`.unity`) |
| `validate [asset]` | Check for broken UI; fails on NEW errors only |
| `screenshots [asset]` | Render UI at every configured resolution |
| `run AgentEdits.<Class>.Run` | Execute an edit script, then auto re-map + validate what it saved |
| `compile` | Check scripts compile (after C# changes) |

### 1. Understand before editing
- Start at `UIAgentMap/INDEX.md`. Read the map of every scene/prefab you will touch
  (`UIAgentMap/scenes/*.md`, `UIAgentMap/prefabs/*.md`). They show the hierarchy with an
  exact address per object, RectTransform layout, every serialized field by property path,
  Button/Toggle/UnityEvent listeners, prefab-instance overrides, and scene scripts wired to UI.
- `UIAgentMap/prefab-usage.md` shows every scene/prefab that instantiates or references a prefab.
- If INDEX.md says a map is stale or was made with unsaved Editor changes, run `map <asset>` first.
- Code that drives the UI: follow the `script:` paths printed next to each component.

### 2. Decide WHERE the change belongs
- Should apply everywhere the prefab is used -> edit the prefab asset (`EditPrefab`).
- Should apply to one scene only -> edit the scene (`EditScene`); on a prefab instance this
  creates a scene override. Deleting/re-parenting objects inside a prefab instance is not
  allowed in a scene - do it in the prefab asset.
- Nested prefab / prefab variant: edit the most specific asset that should own the change.

### 3. Make the change - ONLY through an edit script
- NEVER hand-edit `.unity`, `.prefab`, `.asset` or `.meta` files as text. NEVER use
  `Object.Instantiate` for prefabs in edit scripts (breaks the prefab link).
- Write `Assets/Editor/AgentEdits/Edit_<yyyyMMdd>_<Topic>.cs` in `namespace AgentEdits`,
  a `public static class` with `public static void Run()`, using only the `UIAgentEdit` API:
  `EditPrefab(path, root => ...)`, `EditScene(path, scene => ...)`, `Find(root|scene, "address")`,
  `Get(go, "ComponentType")`, `Set(component, "m_PropertyPath", value)`, `SetText`, `SetActive`,
  `SetName`, `SetRect`, `SetSiblingIndex`, `SetParent`, `CreateChild`, `AddComponent`,
  `RemoveComponent`, `InstantiatePrefab`, `Delete`, `AddListener`, `RemoveListener`, `MarkChanged`.
- Edit scripts compile in their own assembly (`AgentEdits.asmdef`) that sees only Unity and
  UIAgentTools - so refer to project components by name (`Get(go, "LoginController")`), never by
  type. A compile error there can't break the rest of the project.
- Property paths and addresses must be copied from the map files, not guessed.
  Object fields accept an asset path, e.g. `"Assets/Art/ui.png::btn_primary"` for a sprite.
- Run it: `./ui-agent.sh run AgentEdits.Edit_<yyyyMMdd>_<Topic>.Run`. Each EditPrefab/EditScene
  is transactional: it is rejected (nothing saved) if it throws or adds validation errors, and
  the file is restored from backup if post-save verification fails.
- Several related changes -> one script. After it succeeds, move the script out of Assets to
  `UIAgentMap/edit-history/` so it doesn't stay in the project.

### 4. Verify before reporting done
1. The `run` result must be OK with 0 new validation errors.
2. `./ui-agent.sh screenshots <asset>` for each changed asset, then open the PNGs listed in
   `UIAgentMap/screenshots/manifest.md` and check them at every resolution: overflow, clipped
   text, overlaps, safe area, foldable aspect ratios. BLANK images mean the capture failed - say so.
3. Tell the user what changed, which assets were saved, and anything you could not verify
   (runtime-populated content, on-device XR interaction).

### Hard rules
- Unity open with unsaved changes in a scene/prefab you need -> stop and ask the user to save.
- Never run `baseline`, never edit `UIAgentMap/validation-baseline.json` or `config.json`,
  and never delete `UIAgentMap/backups/` without the user's explicit OK.
- Screenshots are a layout check, not proof that XR interaction works on a device.
